    "caption": "The repo server turns Git into manifests, the application controller diffs them against the cluster and syncs, and the API server is only the front door for people and CI.",
    "alt": "A Git repository feeds the repo server, which clones, caches and renders manifests. The application controller asks the repo server for desired state, watches the live state in the target cluster, and applies changes. The ApplicationSet controller generates Application objects that the application controller then reconciles. Users and CI talk to the API server through the UI and CLI; the API server reads status from the controller's results and requests syncs.",
